# Secure Linux TV cleanup - NEVER-TOUCH list.  Written 2026-11-14.
# One shell-style pattern per line (* matches anything). Text after " # " is the reason.
# The tool checks this list before every hide/disable and refuses a match even if you ask.
# The tool never uninstalls system packages at all.
# Sources: https://github.com/ohernandezdev/android-tv-tune/blob/main/data/never-disable.list (MIT),
#          https://github.com/ohernandezdev/android-tv-tune/blob/main/docs/launcher.md,
#          plus extra safety entries added by us (casting, voice, setup, anything named like a system service).

# Android core
android # Android itself
com.android.* # Android system apps, settings, networking, installer, keychain
com.google.android.gms* # Google Play services (almost every app needs it)
com.google.android.gsf* # Google services framework
com.android.vending # Google Play Store
com.google.android.webview* # web engine used by apps
com.google.android.trichromelibrary* # web engine library
com.google.android.permissioncontroller* # app permissions
com.google.android.packageinstaller* # installs apps
com.google.android.ext.* # Google system extensions
com.google.android.modulemetadata # system updates
com.google.android.overlay.* # system look and settings overlays
com.google.android.configupdater # system config updates
com.google.android.gms.* # Google Play services parts

# Casting (the whole point of a Chromecast)
com.google.android.apps.mediashell* # built-in Chromecast receiver
com.google.android.apps.cast* # casting
*.chromecast* # casting
*cast.receiver* # casting

# Remote, voice and input: lose these and the remote stops working
com.google.android.tv.remote* # remote control service
com.google.android.tv.* # Google TV core services
com.google.android.katniss* # voice search and the voice button
com.google.android.inputmethod.* # on-screen keyboard
*.inputmethod.* # keyboards
*.globalkeyoverlay # remote key handling
*.autopair # remote pairing
*bluetooth* # Bluetooth (remote pairing)
*.tvinput # TV inputs
*.tvinput.* # TV inputs
*.systemserver # vendor system service
*.providers.config # vendor configuration

# Home screen, setup and recovery (only the guided "clean home screen" step may touch the first two)
com.google.android.apps.tv.launcherx* # Google TV home screen
com.google.android.tungsten.* # Google TV setup and recovery
com.google.android.tvrecommendations* # home screen recommendations engine
com.google.android.leanbacklauncher* # Android TV home screen
com.google.android.setupwizard* # setup wizard
com.google.android.tv.setupwraith* # setup wizard
*setupwraith* # setup wizard
*setupwizard* # setup wizard
*provision* # provisioning

# Network and settings
*wifi* # Wi-Fi
*networkstack* # networking
*.settings* # settings
*.tethering* # network sharing
*telephony* # phone parts some boxes need

# Vendor chip and system drivers
com.realtek.* # chip maker services
com.mediatek.* # chip maker services
com.amlogic.* # chip maker services
com.tvos # TV operating layer

# The apps this kit installs
me.efesser.flauncher # FLauncher home screen
org.smarttube.* # SmartTube
com.spocky.projengmenu # Projectivy home screen (if you installed your own)
com.google.android.youtube.tv # the normal YouTube app
